WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.007 --> 00:00:04.373
Meet Schematic: a working design reference for interfaces with feeling.

2
00:00:04.373 --> 00:00:08.739
Try the live interaction studies, then search the actual collection.

3
00:00:08.739 --> 00:00:11.358
Every result opens its working example.

4
00:00:11.358 --> 00:00:17.034
We will explore ten collections, including sixteen new animated primitives and navigation patterns.

5
00:00:17.534 --> 00:00:18.264
New here?

6
00:00:18.264 --> 00:00:20.818
Open Guide for a short, optional introduction.

7
00:00:20.818 --> 00:00:25.927
Choose your palette, try a meaningful motion, and learn where the reusable pieces live.

8
00:00:25.927 --> 00:00:31.035
You can close the guide at any point and return whenever you need it.

9
00:00:31.535 --> 00:00:33.786
Foundations makes the decisions visible.

10
00:00:33.786 --> 00:00:38.737
Colour, typography, space, corners, and elevation share one set of tokens.

11
00:00:38.737 --> 00:00:44.139
The default is warm paper and graphite, with a restrained forest accent.

12
00:00:44.139 --> 00:00:48.190
Mono keeps the interface neutral and chart series distinguishable.

13
00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:54.494
The Motion Lab lets you replay and scrub a curve, then adjust a physical spring.

14
00:00:54.494 --> 00:00:57.589
Entry, exit, travel, and confirmation have different jobs.

15
00:00:57.589 --> 00:01:03.005
Reduced motion preserves the same information, and slow motion helps you inspect the details.

16
00:01:03.505 --> 00:01:07.275
Seventy hand-built SVG icons share a grid and stroke weight.

17
00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:10.667
A bell rings, a lid opens, a copy separates.

18
00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:14.813
Search the collection, adjust its size, or play the complete set.

19
00:01:14.813 --> 00:01:17.451
Click an icon to copy its usage.

20
00:01:17.951 --> 00:01:21.636
Components includes the states between idle and done.

21
00:01:21.636 --> 00:01:25.320
These local simulations show success, failure, and retry.

22
00:01:25.320 --> 00:01:29.465
A deliberate hold can be cancelled before it completes.

23
00:01:29.465 --> 00:01:35.452
Tabs, switches, chips, and menus keep their meaning when you use a keyboard.

24
00:01:35.952 --> 00:01:38.235
Primitives adds eight new working studies.

25
00:01:38.235 --> 00:01:40.137
Accordion content opens in place.

26
00:01:40.137 --> 00:01:43.181
Pin a document and its neighbours make room.

27
00:01:43.181 --> 00:01:49.268
Reorder a plan with a keyboard, change a message, roll a number, or turn a card.

28
00:01:49.268 --> 00:01:53.453
Each motion follows your choice, and can change direction halfway through.

29
00:01:53.953 --> 00:01:55.915
Navigation brings eight more patterns.

30
00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:58.661
A shared menu surface follows its selection.

31
00:01:58.661 --> 00:02:04.155
Search a real list, explore a tree, change pages, or choose a dock view.

32
00:02:04.155 --> 00:02:09.649
The stepper validates its fields, and the carousel gives each slide its own place.

33
00:02:09.649 --> 00:02:12.003
Keyboard controls reach the same states.

34
00:02:12.503 --> 00:02:15.968
Forms combines familiar native inputs with useful feedback.

35
00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.133
Validation explains what needs attention.

36
00:02:18.133 --> 00:02:21.165
Pasted verification codes fill all six cells.

37
00:02:21.165 --> 00:02:26.362
The composed profile updates locally, and reset restores your last demo save.

38
00:02:26.362 --> 00:02:29.827
File progress is clearly labelled as a simulation.

39
00:02:30.327 --> 00:02:33.301
Charts draw when the actual plot enters view.

40
00:02:33.301 --> 00:02:35.904
The line leads and its area follows.

41
00:02:35.904 --> 00:02:41.853
Change the period for a fresh trace, or inspect a day with the pointer or keyboard.

42
00:02:41.853 --> 00:02:44.827
All data here is generated for the reference.

43
00:02:45.327 --> 00:02:51.598
Hover a bucket to compare its values, then pin it with a click or a key.

44
00:02:51.598 --> 00:02:53.166
Channel rows reveal contribution.

45
00:02:53.166 --> 00:02:55.910
Donut arcs and their legend respond together.

46
00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:59.829
Progress rings reveal what remains, without hiding their exact targets.

47
00:03:00.329 --> 00:03:02.885
Customer activity is a working table.

48
00:03:02.885 --> 00:03:08.850
Filter the generated accounts and select anywhere in a row, including its empty space.

49
00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.554
The checkmark draws in.

50
00:03:10.554 --> 00:03:15.666
Keyboard selection, sorting, pagination, and a local CSV export complete the flow.

51
00:03:16.166 --> 00:03:19.640
Overlays preserves context when an interface interrupts you.

52
00:03:19.640 --> 00:03:22.246
A card expands into its dialog.

53
00:03:22.246 --> 00:03:25.285
Drawers and sheets start at their edge.

54
00:03:25.285 --> 00:03:32.668
Native modality contains focus, Escape brings you back, and toasts acknowledge an action without stopping the work.

55
00:03:33.168 --> 00:03:35.449
Both palettes support light and dark.

56
00:03:35.449 --> 00:03:39.632
A theme change reveals the complete surface, including the empty background.

57
00:03:39.632 --> 00:03:42.293
The command palette reaches every page quickly.

58
00:03:42.293 --> 00:03:46.476
The same offline file keeps your page state while you explore.

59
00:03:46.976 --> 00:03:52.103
Download a single HTML file, or clone the source and make it your own.

60
00:03:52.103 --> 00:03:55.033
Read the quick start for the reuse path.

61
00:03:55.033 --> 00:04:00.161
Schematic is the working web reference; React, SwiftUI, and Rust adapters are future work.
